     against a baseline of 95 in 100, and the Fisher cutoff is 17. The test
     also enforces a baseline-derived p95 constraint, decided by
     latency/precedence over the 95 baseline latencies and the 17 latencies
     of the samples that passed every functional criterion. With a test of
     17, the p95 is the test's slowest latency, and even the baseline's
     slowest latency would be exceeded by an unchanged service with
     probability 17 / (95 + 17) = 0.152, above alpha 0.05. No baseline rank
     achieves alpha, so there is no threshold: the evaluation is SATURATED,
     carries no threshold-ms and no baseline-rank, and is inconclusive
     (Statistical Companion §12.4.2). A larger baseline is needed.

     The record's verdict is the overall test verdict: the functional
     composite is PASS and the latency verdict is INCONCLUSIVE, so the test
     is INCONCLUSIVE, triggered by the p95 latency constraint. -->
